  "notes": "Source: FRCC current Catalog 2026-2027 (official SmartCatalogIQ), 'LPN to ADN Associate of Applied Science' (page notes the award is currently known as 'Nursing Advanced Placement Bridge Program LPN to ADN' and has been requested to be retitled to 'LPN to ADN AAS', pending CCCS/HLC/ED approval). Hand-transcribed 2026-10-06 from officially published tables (browser search-index path; shell egress down). Structure as published: a 50-credit 'LPN Transfer Credit' block (22 cr block transfer from completed LPN program + 28 cr general education) followed by a 3-semester full-time My Academic Plan (24.5 cr nursing coursework); total 74.5 cr. Catalog's own Important Program Note still says the 24.5 nursing credits are 'found in Semesters 2-4' (stale wording from the prior 4-semester layout) while the published MAP tables show First/Second/Third Semester only — transcribed as published, 3+12.5+9=24.5. The Nursing AAS page's LPN-option note describes 21 block + 29 gen-ed + 21.5 = 71.5 (+3 NUR 2002 = 74.5); the dedicated LPN page (authoritative here) states 22 block + 28 gen-ed + 24.5 = 74.5.",
